  "question": {
    "text": "A function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> satisfies <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> with condition <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math> is equal to"
  },
